WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:07.140
North Korea is officially the most corrupt
country in the World.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:13.550
The Corruption Perceptions Index ranks every
country in the world from 0 to 100, based

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:20.710
on how corrupt it is, with a score of 0 being
very corrupt and 100 meaning very clean.

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:26.250
Every year North Korea ties with Somalia for
last place.

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:38.120
Let's uncover the most disturbing facts about
the World's favourite hermit kingdom.

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:43.940
North Korea, or more officially known as the
Democratic Peoples Republic of Korea, has

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:51.620
the fourth largest army in the world, with
1.2 million active members, not far behind

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:56.280
America with it's military of 1.4 million.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:01:00.640
There are 28 state approved haircuts in North
Korea.

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:04.320
Women are allowed to choose from one of 18
styles.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:09.080
Married women are instructed to choose shorter
styles, whilst single ladies are permitted

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:12.119
to let loose with a longer style.

00:01:12.119 --> 00:01:18.470
Men on the other hand are allowed to choose
from 10 state approved hair cuts, all of which

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:19.939
are short.

00:01:19.939 --> 00:01:27.390
All North Korean men are prohibited from growing
their hair longer than 5 centimetres.

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:32.930
North Korea has an impressive 100% literacy
rate.

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:39.700
Literacy is defined as individuals aged 15
and over who can read and write.

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:50.890
There are 25,554 kilometres of roads in North
Korea, but only 724 km are paved, that's a

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:54.640
measly 2.83%.

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:57.409
The Korean Demilitarised Zone, or DMZ.

00:01:57.409 --> 00:02:05.220
Is a strip of land 250 kilometres long that
separates South Korea from North Korea.

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:10.030
It was setup as a neutral zone where the two
countries can safely discuss matters, at the

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:13.370
end of Korean War in 1953.

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:18.700
Despite its name, it is the most heavily militarised
border in the world.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:25.530
Soldiers guarding the DMZ are ordered to shoot
anyone trying to sneak in our out of the country.

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:30.080
Making China the most popular escape route
for North Koreans.

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:33.620
80% of defectors are women.

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:40.849
But an unlikely good has come out of such
a heavily militarised border, the Korean DMZ

00:02:40.849 --> 00:02:47.060
strip is home to some of the most critically
endangered species of animals and plants on

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:48.220
Earth.

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:53.580
Whom have found an unlikely haven, protected
from any human contact.

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:59.970
Extremely rare species such as the Korean
Tiger, the elusive Amur leopard and Asiatic

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:06.520
black bear have all found a home here amongst
the landmines and listening posts.

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:15.890
Ecologists have identified some 2,900 plant
species, 70 types of mammals and 320 kinds

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:19.440
of birds within this narrow strip of land.

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:25.690
The South Korea government has campaigned
to UNESCO numerous times to turn the DMZ into

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:33.530
a nature reserve to protect the endangered
animals, but every time North Korea has declined

00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:36.580
to make such an agreement.

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:42.900
In the 50s, North Korea built Kijong-Dong
on North Korea's side of the DMZ, so it was

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:45.660
easily visible from South Korea.

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:52.260
Which North Korea claimed was the perfect
city, the city supposedly contained a childcare

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:58.129
centre, kindergarten, primary and secondary
schools, and a hospital.

00:03:58.129 --> 00:04:04.459
The idea was to make the city appear so attractive
that it enticed South Koreans to defect to

00:04:04.459 --> 00:04:06.239
North Korea.

00:04:06.239 --> 00:04:12.190
However, after observation from the South
Korean side of the DMZ, it became obvious

00:04:12.190 --> 00:04:20.270
that the city is actually completely uninhabited,
and has remained so ever since it was built.

00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:24.130
It has since come to be known as 'Propaganda
Village'.

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:31.020
In the 1980s the South Korean government built
a 98 metre tall flagpole on the south side

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:33.760
of the DMZ, close to the border.

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:40.160
The North Korean government responded by building
an ever taller one in Kijong-Dong, in what

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:43.160
some have called the "flagpole war".

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:49.190
At the time it was the second tallest flagpole
in the world.

00:04:49.190 --> 00:04:57.280
In the last 60 years, over 23,000 North Koreans
have defected to South Korea.

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:02.240
Whereas only two South Koreans have gone north
of the border.

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:09.030
North Korea has its own operating system called
Red Star OS, a fork of linux.

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:14.450
Most of the software on there, such as the
web browser, text editor and firewall are

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:18.669
custom programs written by North Korea.

00:05:18.669 --> 00:05:27.560
In 1974, Kim Il-Sung took 1,000 Volvo sedans
from Sweden to North Korea and never paid

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:28.880
for them.

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:37.120
In 2013 current North Korean leader Kim Jong-Un
executed his uncle along with five of his

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:44.169
aides by locking them in a cage and feeding
them to a starving pack of 120 dogs.

00:05:44.169 --> 00:05:49.920
But what had Kim's uncle done to deserve such
a horrific demise?

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:57.440
Kim accused his uncle of mismanaging the economy,
corruption, womanising and taking drugs.

00:05:57.440 --> 00:06:04.560
Marijuana is completely legal in North Korea
and is not even classified as a drug.

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:07.819
It is commonly used for medicinal purposes.

00:06:07.819 --> 00:06:15.720
North Korea is the only nation on Earth to
currently have a US Navy ship captured.

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:21.740
It isn't 2015 in North Korea, it is the year
104.

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:30.000
Counted after the birth of Kim Jong Un's grandfather,
and founder of the DPRK, Kim Il-Sung.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:34.030
North Korea is home to the world's largest
stadium.

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:39.199
The impressive May Day Stadium seats 150,000
people.

00:06:39.199 --> 00:06:44.880
It is home to the annual Arirang games, which
is one of the most spectacular displays of

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:49.229
coordination and choreography on Earth.

00:06:49.229 --> 00:06:57.090
The Ryugyong Hotel in North Korea is a 105
story building that for 20 years held the

00:06:57.090 --> 00:07:00.190
title of the world's tallest hotel.

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:07.221
Construction began in 1987, but was halted
before it was finished in 1992, as North Korea

00:07:07.221 --> 00:07:12.990
entered a period of economic crisis following
the fall of the Soviet Union.

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:19.449
The monstrosity now towers over Pyongyang
and stands completely empty.

00:07:19.449 --> 00:07:25.150
The only people allowed to own vehicles in
North Korea are the military and government

00:07:25.150 --> 00:07:26.690
officials.

00:07:26.690 --> 00:07:32.840
Transport in general is tightly controlled,
North Korean citizens are generally restricted

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:38.190
from travelling anywhere at all, even inside
their own country.

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:46.110
North Korea's space agency is called "NADA",
which in Spanish means "nothing".

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:50.490
It stands for National Aerospace Development
Administration.

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:55.030
The program only has a 20% success rate.

00:07:55.030 --> 00:08:02.980
Wearing jeans is illegal in North Korea because
denim symbolises the DPRK's enemy, the United

00:08:02.980 --> 00:08:04.360
States.

00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:11.300
Every 5 years North Korea holds a general
election, in which the ballots paper lists

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:14.000
only one candidate.

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:23.319
In 2012 North Korea officially announced that
it had discovered a unicorn lair.

00:08:23.319 --> 00:08:30.020
The DPRK's official news agency released a
statement claiming they had found a cave 200

00:08:30.020 --> 00:08:36.219
metres from Pyongyang City, with a rectangular
rock in front of it with the words "Unicorn

00:08:36.219 --> 00:08:39.580
Lair" conveniently carved into it.

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:46.180
They believe the unicorn was rode by an ancient
Korean king named King Tongmyong.

00:08:46.180 --> 00:08:49.810
North Korea is dotted with prison labor camps.

00:08:49.810 --> 00:08:55.959
Where prisoners are reportedly subjected to
horrific inhumane treatment.

00:08:55.959 --> 00:09:01.870
Prisoners of these concentration camps suffer
a level of slavery, torture and experimentation

00:09:01.870 --> 00:09:04.570
comparable with the holocaust.

00:09:04.570 --> 00:09:10.330
Although North Korea denies the existence
of such camps, insider sources claim there

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:18.029
are 16 such camps, home to 200,000 prisoners.

00:09:18.029 --> 00:09:22.980
North Korea also has a three generations of
punishment law.

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:29.470
This means that anyone sent to a prison camp
is sent along with their entire family, regardless

00:09:29.470 --> 00:09:32.839
if they were involved in the crime or not.

00:09:32.839 --> 00:09:38.980
Also any family members born whilst in prison
will live their entire lives there, as well

00:09:38.980 --> 00:09:43.260
as any children they may have whilst in prison.

00:09:43.260 --> 00:09:49.880
North Koreans are subject to a six day work
week, as well as a seventh day of supposed

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:55.530
"volunteer" work, which is also strictly enforced.

00:09:55.530 --> 00:10:00.890
Meaning North Koreans have virtually no free
time.

00:10:00.890 --> 00:10:06.269
Official records show that Kim Jong il learnt
to walk at the age of three weeks, and was

00:10:06.269 --> 00:10:08.399
talking at eight weeks.

00:10:08.399 --> 00:10:17.490
Whilst studying at Kim il Sung university,
he reportedly wrote 1,500 books over a period

00:10:17.490 --> 00:10:21.860
of three years, along with six full operas.

00:10:21.860 --> 00:10:28.100
According to his official biography, all of
his operas are "better than any in the history

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:29.630
of music."

00:10:29.630 --> 00:10:35.700
It is also written in Kim Jong il's biography
that he was born under a double rainbow, and

00:10:35.700 --> 00:10:40.140
to mark his birth there was a new star and
a swallow in the sky.

00:10:40.140 --> 00:10:45.570
It is also written that he could control the
weather and make it rain on command, depending

00:10:45.570 --> 00:10:47.510
on his mood.

00:10:47.510 --> 00:10:52.690
In fact, the list of questionable claims and
feats of prowess surrounding the former North

00:10:52.690 --> 00:10:55.279
Korean leader are endless.

00:10:55.279 --> 00:11:00.500
School children are required to learn everything
about their current leader as well as his

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:02.660
two predecessors.

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:20.309
Even if the so called facts may be a bit on
the fabricated side.

